# `var K = 0; lib.KINDS = { FIRST: K++, SECOND: K++, THIRD: K++ }; K = lib.KINDS`, and `lib` has left the program's sight: the inferred type of the variable is a number, what is proven of it is nothing; every `K.FIRST` behind it was read closed ("holds primitives too"). In a function that is not checked the objects that Link holds to lie in the variable are expected in place of an inferred type that holds no object: the test stands in front of the loop, the reads go out of slots.
